WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.600
Most people thought it was impossible to get past him.

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:02.520
I beat him every time.

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:04.030
You just punch when he gets dizzy.

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:04.400
Really?

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:05.880
I mean, duh.

00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:06.660
Everyone knows that.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:07.380
Tell us about Friday.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:08.720
I had a late afternoon surgery.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:09.860
Simple gum graft.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.380
wrapped around 6: 00, and then Robert and I talked after.

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:13.620
And who else was in the office?

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:17.700
Our hygienist and anesthesiologist had gone home, and Grace, who usually locks up,

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:19.980
had left early because her grandson had a school play.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:21.460
So it was just you and Robert.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:21.900
No witnesses?

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:22.560
That's lucky.

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:25.220
It wasn't lucky because there was nothing to witness.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.600
Robert just wanted to talk about firing one of our office assistants, Cheryl.

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:31.040
And that's all you discussed?

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:31.580
Yeah.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:32.140
Nothing else?

00:00:32.580 --> 00:00:34.060
Zero other subjects were mentioned?

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:35.730
Not even how gross gum grafts are?

00:00:35.740 --> 00:00:36.660
They're really not that gross.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.360
About the gum graft thing, and about the meeting.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:41.360
We just talked about Cheryl.

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:42.160
Right.

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:44.470
And, of course, there's no way for me to check if that's true,

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:46.940
because whoever took Robert's phone wiped all of his calendars.

00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:49.260
Except.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:51.060
it was all backed up on his home laptop.

00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:53.460
Would you like to hear what he said the meeting was about?

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:57.020
7: 00 p.m. Talked with Philip about.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:58.120
Missing meds.

00:00:58.580 --> 00:00:58.953
Ooh.

00:00:58.953 --> 00:01:00.240
Did I get that right?

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:01.380
Uh, yeah.

00:01:01.980 --> 00:01:05.360
But missing meds hardly sounds like firing Cheryl, so maybe you want to explain.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:06.940
He thought Cheryl was stealing Diazepam.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.320
That's why he wanted to fire her.

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:09.240
Any other questions?

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:11.540
Uh.

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:13.720
Boy, you really thought you had him with that one, huh?

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:14.120
Well, I.

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:15.840
You got so excited for it.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:17.710
Let me guess, you, practiced that notebook flip?

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:18.580
Well, yes, obviously.

00:01:18.980 --> 00:01:22.340
I'd like to move on, unless you have any other big revelations in here.

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:22.940
Let's see.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:26.320
From Gomez: Dear Morticia, I feel so happy when I'm wit ya.

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:28.440
I was just spit balling wedding vows there.
